  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The team has expanded to include five new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing (including Mike Chen and Lisa Ray). Key updates include a budget increase for compliance to $55,000 and an approved $15,000 training budget. Security protocols are being updated in January to include multi-factor authentication and encryption. The project is seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by November and exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. Additionally, a detailed assessment of similar projects is recommended."
